        <mxCell id="p_ret_r7_c2" value="Undo a bad publish quickly" style="shape=partialRectangle;connectable=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;overflow=hidden;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;fontColor=#143642;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="p_ret_r7">
          <mxGeometry x="540" width="480" height="34" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="480" height="34" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p_reload" value="&lt;b style='font-size:20px'&gt;Reload policy: one bad day D&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Land the corrected file under &lt;b&gt;ingest_dt=D&lt;/b&gt; as a new version. The bad file stays, marked superseded.&lt;br&gt;2. Overwrite the Silver partitions built from that ingest (&lt;b&gt;sale_dt&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;snapshot_dt&lt;/b&gt;; masters are full).&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;FCT_SALES&lt;/b&gt;: merge on (TRANSACTION_ID, LINE_NUM); recompute &lt;b&gt;AGG&lt;/b&gt; only for the DAY_KY values touched.&lt;br&gt;4. &lt;b&gt;FCT_INVENTORY&lt;/b&gt;: delete + insert WHERE SNAPSHOT_DT = D.&lt;br&gt;5. &lt;b&gt;FCT_PRICE&lt;/b&gt;: re-derive periods from snapshot D onward for changed item and location pairs.&lt;br&gt;6. &lt;b&gt;SCD2 dims&lt;/b&gt;: undo versions opened or closed on D, then re-apply. DIM_CUSTOMER: SCD1 merge.&lt;br&gt;7. Re-run gates G7 to G10, then publish. Every step is idempotent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why it works:&lt;/b&gt; ingest_dt keeps every landing; day partitions (sale_dt, snapshot_dt, DAY_KY, SNAPSHOT_DT) limit the rewrite to day D; FCT_PRICE is unpartitioned so a multi-day period is never split." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#143642;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;arcSize=4;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=17;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2700" y="3300" width="1500" height="414" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p_dep" value="&lt;b style='font-size:20px'&gt;Departure from the reference architecture&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;DIM_DAY is seeded straight into Gold&lt;/b&gt; (green dashed line) instead of flowing through Bronze and Silver.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The calendar is generated deterministically (DAY_KY = YYYYMMDD). There is no source system and nothing raw to keep or clean, so two extra copies would add no audit value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Traceability: the generator script and seed_dim_day.csv are version controlled." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#143642;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;arcSize=4;fillColor=#ECF8E5;strokeColor=#82B366;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=17;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4320" y="3300" width="900" height="414" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FkrYSAVYgd9Qhf3JwcHr-1" parent="1" style="shape=table;startSize=30;container=1;collapsible=1;childLayout=tableLayout;fixedRows=1;rowLines=0;fontStyle=1;align=center;resizeLast=1;html=1;fillColor=#FAE5C7;strokeColor=#0F8B8D;rounded=0;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontColor=#143642;" value="Legend - Table" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="230" x="5340" y="3300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
